    "current_example": {
      "math_academy_id": "e-14490",
      "problem": "What number is missing from the multiplication problem below?\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14130082/assets/69f859c61c693f7ece01fef8f829fdc772acae77e90be97b7b093fb9849acc95.png)",
      "worked_solution": "We have $\\dfrac{1}{2}$ on the left and $\\dfrac{1}{6}$ on the right.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14130082/assets/dcb89325ddd68043c9edf2f595a7a7d89b3ba078bbb1805af7bea58867f627b6.png)\n\nThe shape on the right-hand side is split into $\\color{blue}3$ equal parts by horizontal lines. So, the shaded part on the left is $\\color{blue}3$ times larger than the shaded part on the right. \n\nTherefore, the multiplication problem shown is:\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{1}{2} \\times \\dfrac{1}{\\color{blue}{3}} = \\dfrac{1}{6}\n$$\n\nSo, the missing number is $\\color{blue}3.$",
